        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "The implementation is complete and working. The function `run_tasks` is in `/app/run.py` and can be imported with `from run import run_tasks`. \n\n**Summary of features:**\n- **Concurrency limiting** via `asyncio.Semaphore` with `max_concurrent` parameter\n- **Graceful shutdown** handling for SIGINT/SIGTERM (KeyboardInterrupt) - running tasks get cancelled but their cleanup code (in `except asyncio.CancelledError` blocks) runs to completion\n- **Error isolation** - exceptions in one task don't stop others\n- **Edge case handling** - empty task list, invalid `max_concurrent` values\n- **Cross-platform** - handles Windows where `add_signal_handler` may not be available",
